 "summary": "The new module sits at `EpsilonEridani/QFT/Jets/Observable/SoftSafety.lean`, the directory the JetsAndEventShapes roadmap assigns to safety and counterexamples (`roadmap/.../JetsAndEventShapes/README.md:79`), and nothing in it can move earlier: `Observable/Basic.lean` is stated for topological codomains and `Counterexamples.lean` has no normed dependency, so the multiplicity and leading-energy soft-safety lemmas must live downstream of both. All three imports are specific and used (`ContinuousLinearMap.isBigO_id` from `Normed/Operator/Asymptotics`, `LinearMap.toContinuousBilinearMap` from `FiniteDimensionBilinear`, `particleMultiplicity`/`leadingEnergy` from `Counterexamples`).",
